23. Core Research Hypotheses (Falsifiable)

The primary hypotheses are:

· H1 (Gap Reliability): A gap-driven, evidence-grounded question-generation architecture produces questions with higher expert-validated GapPrecision than conventional prompt-driven LLM question generation.
· H2 (Novelty): The gap-driven architecture produces questions with a lower rediscovery rate than prompt-driven generation, controlling for domain.
· H3 (Diversity): The gap-driven architecture produces structurally more diverse question sets than prompt-driven generation.
· H4 (Testability): Questions produced by the gap-driven architecture are at least as testable as those produced by prompt-driven generation.

Absolute Success Criteria (falsifiable):

· GapPrecision $\geq 0.7$ on SPDB Category 1.
· RediscoveryRate $\leq 0.2$.
· Falsifiability rate $\geq 0.8$.

These thresholds are provisional and to be calibrated with domain experts.

