|                                                                                 |
|  F and R are predicates over KG states, evaluable in the symbolic core.         |
|  F(g,KG) = true  => gap is not genuine (dissolved)                              |
|  R(g,KG) = true  => gap has been answered (resolved)                            |
|  Axiom: ¬(F(KG) ∧ R(KG)) for all KG                                             |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

Explanation: The gap tuple is the core data structure. The predicates F and R distinguish between a gap that was never genuine (dissolution) and one that has been answered (resolution).

