I.9 Structural Similarity Check for Novelty and Diversity

```
  Question q1                    Question q2
       |                              |
       v                              v
  Extract structural signature: Extract structural signature:
  G1 = (V1, E1, labels)         G2 = (V2, E2, labels)
       |                              |
       +--------------+---------------+
                      |
                      v
        Compute similarity:
        - Normalized graph edit distance d_GED(G1,G2)
        - Jaccard index of causal signatures J(S1,S2)
                      |
                      v
        Decision:
        if d_GED < θ1  OR  J > θ2  -> "structurally similar"
        else -> "structurally distinct"
```

Explanation: The same structural comparison function is used for novelty detection and diversity enforcement, ensuring consistency. Thresholds θ1 and θ2 are domain-specific.

