I.10 Scientific Problem Discovery Benchmark (SPDB) Structure

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
| SPDB Instance: B_i = (Corpus, Data, KnownKnowledge, HiddenProblem)|
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                                                                  |
| Four Categories:                                                 |
|                                                                  |
| 1. Historical Cases                                              |
|    - Problem recognized & solved in real history                 |
|    - System given literature only before discovery date          |
|                                                                  |
| 2. Contemporary Open Problems                                    |
|    - From open problem lists, conjectures, review articles       |
|                                                                  |
| 3. Synthetic Gaps                                                |
|    - Knowledge artificially removed from a complete corpus       |
|    - (edge removal) tests detection capacity                     |
|                                                                  |
| 4. Neglect Cases                                                 |
|    - Important questions systematically overlooked               |
|    - Tests accessibility-based novelty                           |
|                                                                  |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
| System receives available info, must output candidate question q_i|
| Performance measured by GapPrecision, RediscoveryRate, Diversity |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

Explanation: The SPDB is designed to evaluate the architecture's ability to identify genuine research questions, not just solve given ones.

